      {
        "Id": "81393432d8574a74a5284b20be79f8de",
        "Title": "HOW TO USE:  open the floor plan.  PICTURE: give the plan picture / PDF (1) - grid lines ending in round bubbles are found, the text in each bubble is read and becomes the grid name, the size comes from the dimensions written between the grids (or type the first grid spacing in 3).  CAD: leave 1 empty - the grid lines of the CAD linked in the plan are used (GRID / AXIS layers, names from the bubble text).  Run first with 12 = False and read the RESULT: names GUESSED and spacings marked ~ must be checked - correct them in 4-7.  Then 12 = True.  Run again = nothing doubled.",
